# MORPHER — Zero-Trust Metamorphic AST Morpher

File: guide/Morpher.oot
User wiki. Canonical URL: https://openooda.org/guide/#Morpher.oot

[Home](Home.oot) [Start](Use.oot) [Language](Language.oot) [Commands](Options.oot) [Capabilities](Safety.oot) [How it works](Limits.oot)

## 1. What the Morpher is

The Zero-Trust Metamorphic AST Morpher is an ahead-of-time diversification and binary fortification engine built directly into openOODA.

It takes any valid `.oo` source program and applies multi-stage mathematical and topological transformations at compile time.
Every compilation produces a radically unique cryptographic binary hash and execution layout while guaranteeing:

1. **100% Semantic Equivalence**: All functions compute identical return values and pass all verification beats.
2. **Zero Ambient Authority**: Morphed routines cannot mint capability tokens or escape sandboxes.
3. **Zero Runtime Overhead**: Obfuscation and layout diversification happen ahead-of-time during C emission.

## 2. Core Transformation Stages

### 2.1 Control Flow Flattening (Chenxi Wang Obfuscation)
Hierarchical `if/else` and `while` loop trees are decomposed into flat basic blocks governed by a centralized state-machine switch dispatcher.
Decompilers (IDA Pro, Ghidra) cannot reconstruct the original algorithmic control flow.

### 2.2 Dynamic Basic Block Permutation
Basic blocks are shuffled across physical memory using a cryptographic entropy seed.
Unconditional branch fixups are injected automatically to preserve original execution flow while invalidating static binary signatures.

### 2.3 Number-Theoretic Opaque Predicates
Injects algebraic identities (e.g. `(x * (x + 1)) % 2 == 0`) and quadratic non-residues mod 7 (`(7*y^2 - 1) % 7 == (x^2) % 7` is always false).
Forces exponential state explosion in symbolic execution engines and automated SMT solvers (angr, Z3).

### 2.4 Compile-Time String Encryption
String literals and sensitive constant tables are encrypted at build time using dynamic rolling XOR keys.
Stack-transient decrypters reconstruct strings in local stack frames only for the duration of the call and zero memory immediately after.

### 2.5 Anti-ROP / Anti-JOP Gadget Elimination
Scans intermediate bytecode streams for unintended `0xC3` (`ret`) or `0xFF 0x25` (`jmp`) byte alignments.
Injects safe multi-byte NOP padders to break exploitable ROP gadget sequences before native binary generation.

### 2.6 Decoy Function & Dead Code Injection
Synthesizes capability-starved decoy routines and unreachable dummy blocks connected via opaque false predicates to waste reverse-engineering time.

## 3. Zero-Trust Security Guarantees

The Morpher strictly enforces all openOODA Zero-Trust invariants:

- **Unforgeable Tokens**: Morphed dispatchers cannot synthesize `&FsReadCap`, `&FsWriteCap`, or `&ProcessCap`.
- **Capability Scoping**: Decoy code paths possess zero ambient tokens and fail closed if invoked.
- **Contract Preservation**: All `requires`, `ensures`, and `spec` contract clauses are verified before transformation.

## 4. How to Use

From the command line:

```
ooda morph src/main.oo -o build/morphed.oo --entropy 83921
ooda run build/morphed.oo
```

Or via the compiler pass:

```
oodac emit-c --metamorphic src/main.oo > build/out.c
gcc -O0 -Iruntime runtime/chs_rt.c build/out.c -o build/bin -lm
```

